  "raw": {
    "https://tcnj.taleo.net/careersection/00_ex_faculty/jobdetail.ftl?job=26000830": {
      "title": "Visiting Assistant Professor-Chemistry",
      "description": "Job Description - Visiting Assistant Professor-Chemistry (26000830) Go to the main content section. Return to Careers Home Employment Opportunities Faculty Adjunct Faculty Staff/Administrative Internal Employment Student Employment Welcome. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Advanced Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Visiting Assistant Professor-Chemistry (26000830) Job Description Visiting Assistant Professor-Chemistry - ( 26000830 ) Description Appointment Type: Non-Tenure Track State Title: Assistant Professor Bargaining Unit: AFT Employment Type: 35 hours per week/Full-Time Expected Start Date:  January 9, 2027 End Date: June 11, 2027 Compensation: Range 22/ $86,720.75 - $ 93,659.67 About TCNJ The College of New Jersey (TCNJ) is a highly selective institution that is consistently recognized as one of the top comprehensive colleges in the nation. Founded in 1855 as the New Jersey State Normal School, TCNJ maintains the eighth highest four-year graduation rate among all public colleges and universities. It is ranked by Money as one of the top 15 public colleges “most likely to pay off financially,” and U.S. News & World Report rates it the No. 1 public institution among regional universities in the northeast. About the Department: The Chemistry Department has 13 full-time faculty members, 9 of whom are tenure-track, and approximately 120 majors. We occupy a recently expanded and renovated Chemistry Building, which is part of TCNJ’s six-building STEM Complex, providing tremendous opportunities for interdisciplinary collaboration. The Chemistry Department offers state-of-the-art teaching and research facilities with extensive instrumentation (see: science.tcnj.edu/about/facilities-labs ) . TCNJ’s Department of Chemistry offers a Bachelor of Science in Chemistry degree with specializations in Biochemistry, Materials Chemistry, and Secondary Education. The Bachelor of Science in Chemistry degree can be Amer ican Chemical Society ( ACS) certified. Over 80% of our majors participate in one or more semesters of research with a Chemistry faculty member. A large percentage of our undergraduates go on to earn Ph.D.s in Chemistry and related fields. In the past five years, the department was awarded over $3 million in external grants and has produced more than 4 0 peer-reviewed papers or book chapters.  TCNJ faculty and students are very active with the American Chemical Society and recently hosted the Middle Atlantic Regional Meeting (MARM) in 2022 with the Trenton Local Section. For more information about the department, visit chemistry.tcnj.edu . Position Overview: The Department of Chemistry at The College of New Jersey (TCNJ) invites applications for a Visiting Assistant Professor, starting Spring 2027. The successful candidate will have a Ph.D. in one of the Chemistry subdisciplines (Analytical, Biochemistry, Inorganic, Organic, or Physical) or a closely related field, with teaching experience in introductory, analytical, biochemistry, inorganic, organic, or physical chemistry. We invite applicants who are committed to high-quality teaching and mentorship with undergraduate students and possess a commitment to using active-learning pedagogies in lecture and laboratory settings. We encourage applications from candidates with a wide range of professional backgrounds and experiences, including mid-career applicants. Teaching responsibilities will include General Chemistry and one or more other courses, including Organic Chemistry, Analytical Chemistry, Biochemistry, Thermodynamics, and/or our General Organic Biochemistry (GOB) course for nursing students. These teaching assignments are typically scheduled during the day, but may on occasion require instruction of an evening course section. Preference will be given to applicants whose background enables them to teach upper-level advanced courses– some examples include organic synthesis, instrumental analysis, bioanalytical chemistry, process chemistry, kinetics, pharmacology and toxicology, bioinformatics, proteomics, or medicinal chemistry. Ideal candidates should have an interest in developing and implementing high-impact teaching pedagogies that use active learning and student-centered approaches, as well as laboratory instruction that focuses on inquiry-based learning. The Department continues to enhance its General, Organic, and GOB chemistry curricula, and its B.S. degree track, which includes ACS-certification and materials science and biochemistry specializations. Please visit the Department's website for information on its curriculum, faculty members, and their research interests: https://chemistry.tcnj.edu Applicants will be expected to actively participate in departmental activities, including departmental and faculty committees in addition to their 24 FWH/10 month teaching load . The Department of Chemistry and the School of Science are also deeply invested in the professional development of all of our faculty. As members of the TCNJ community, faculty and staff benefit from professional development resources, including Center for Excellence in Teaching and Learning (CETL) instructional mini-grants, pedagogical workshops, and campus-wide training programs supported by Academic Affairs and Human Resources. Persons with disabilities may request reasonable accommodations in order to perform the essential functions of the position. If the requested accommodation(s) cannot be made because it would cause the employer undue hardship, the applicant may not be eligible for the position. Employer Qualifications Employment at TCNJ is contingent upon the successful completion of an applicable background check, reference checks, and verification of identity and authorization to work in the United States (Form I-9). Accommodation: Applicants who require a reasonable accommodation to apply or interview should contact hr@tcnj.edu . Employee Benefits As a member of The College of New Jersey Community, you will be a part of an exciting and rewarding public college career. Eligible full-time employees will be able to take advantage of a generous benefits package that includes health, welfare, and retirement benefits, including: Comprehensive benefit plans covering medical, dental and prescription plans Generous leave entitlements program and Energy Savings Program Employee and dependent Tuition Waiver and Reimbursement Program Pension, retirement, and deferred compensation plans, group life insurance Employee Assistance Program (EAP) Employee affinity groups New Jersey State Employee Discount Program (Pet insurance, cell phone plan discounts, discounted amusement park tickets, etc.) Access to extensive learning opportunities To view a comprehensive list of benefits available to employees, visit our Health Benefits Plans and Programs page to learn more! How to Apply A pplicants should compile a single PDF file containing the items listed below. Apply online at the following link and upload a single PDF file to the resume section of the application : Letter of application indicating how the candidate's background aligns with the advertised position, Curriculum vitae, Statement of Teaching and Mentoring Philosophy: A statement outlining the candidate’s philosophy on undergraduate teaching, student mentoring, and their alignment with the educational and strategic goals of the College. Candidates may draw upon experience gained through direct classroom instruction, laboratory supervision, industrial team leadership, technical mentoring, or other relevant experiences. The statement should discuss the candidate’s abilities to teach upper-level chemistry courses as well as their commitment to inclusive teaching practices (2-3 pages). Unofficial copies of all graduate transcripts, and a List of three references with contact information who can speak to the applicant's potential for teaching excellence, organizational skills, and ability to work as part of a team . ( If selected for a site visit, references will be contacted.) Review of complete applications will begin on October 22, 2026 . The College is committed to fostering a welcoming and inclusive campus community that respects and uplifts individuals from all backgrounds. We value the varied perspectives, experiences, and talents of all members of our community and strive to create an environment where everyone has equitable access to opportunities for success. As an equal opportunity employer, we comply with all applicable federal and state laws regarding nondiscrimination and affirmative action. We encourage applications from individuals whose lived experiences and professional interests align with our institutional mission of academic excellence, access, and integrity. Primary Location : Chemistry Building - Chemistry Work Locations : Chemistry Building - Chemistry 2000 Pennington Rd Ewing Township 08628 Job : Faculty Organization : The College of New Jersey Job Posting : Oct 13, 2026, 1:26:26 PM Copyright © 2020"
    },
    "https://tcnj.taleo.net/careersection/00_ex_faculty/jobdetail.ftl?job=26001064": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Job Description - Assistant Professor - Interpersonal Communication (26001064) Go to the main content section. Return to Careers Home Employment Opportunities Faculty Adjunct Faculty Staff/Administrative Internal Employment Student Employment Welcome. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Advanced Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Assistant Professor - Interpersonal Communication (26001064) Job Description Assistant Professor - Interpersonal Communication - ( 26001064 ) Description Appointment Type: Tenure Track State Title: Assistant Professor Bargaining Unit: AFT Employment Type: 35-hour work week/Full-time Expected Term : 8/9/2027 - 6/8/2030 Compensation: Range 22, $93,659.67 About TCNJ The College of New Jersey (TCNJ) is a highly selective institution that is consistently recognized as one of the top comprehensive colleges in the nation. Founded in 1855 as the New Jersey State Normal School, TCNJ maintains the eighth highest four-year graduation rate among all public colleges and universities. It is ranked by Money as one of the top 15 public colleges “most likely to pay off financially,” and U.S. News & World Report rates it the No. 1 public institution among regional universities in the northeast. Position Overview The Department of Communication, Journalism, and Film (CJF) at The College of New Jersey (TCNJ) invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position in technology-mediated interpersonal communication. We seek an outstanding teacher-scholar whose research and teaching expertise centers on the intersection of interpersonal or relational communication and technology-mediated communication. The successful candidate’s research program should keep interpersonal or relational communication at its core, even as it engages with technology. Examples of research programs that align with this position include how technology-mediated communication shapes identity and/or personal and relational well-being; how communication processes such as conflict management, self-disclosure, and social support unfold through technology-mediated channels; and how technology-mediated communication is used within, or influences, couples and families. Research centered on digital media, mass communication, or technology in society that does not also engage relational or interpersonal communication falls outside the scope of this search. Consistent with TCNJ’s teacher-scholar model, the successful candidate will teach undergraduate courses including Introduction to Communication Theory, Interpersonal Communication, and Research Methods, along with technology-mediated interpersonal communication courses that reflect their research expertise, while developing curriculum that bridges theory and practice. They will also mentor undergraduate students in professional development and research. In their research role, the faculty member will conduct original research in technology-mediated interpersonal communication, publish in peer-reviewed journals and other appropriate venues, present at professional conferences, and collaborate with departmental colleagues. Service expectations include participating in departmental, school, and college-level service, contributing to professional organizations and the broader academic community, and engaging in community outreach as appropriate. About the Department of Communication, Journalism, and Film The Department of Communication, Journalism, and Film (CJF) is one of the four departments within TCNJ’s School of the Arts and Communication. The department offers three majors: Communication Studies, Film and Television, and Journalism and Professional Writing, serving over 250 major students. There are four specializations in the Communication Studies major: Emerging Communication Technologies, Health Communication, Interpersonal and Strategic Communication, and Mass Media and Social Media. Aligned with the School’s mission, CJF cultivates analytical, critical, and creative thinking while fostering conscientious global citizenship and lifelong learning. Through integrated teaching and scholarship, we prepare students to make meaningful contributions to their communities and chosen careers. Our departmental mission centers on maximizing student engagement in the discovery and creation of knowledge, art, and information. We encourage independent initiative and inquiry while instilling a passion for lifelong learning. Our faculty serve as active professional scholars and writers who significantly advance knowledge and understanding in their respective fields. Additionally, CJF faculty prepare students to engage thoughtfully with a range of perspectives, experiences, and communities, equipping them with the knowledge and skills necessary to serve and strengthen the communities in which they will live and work. For more information about the departments, please visit https://cjf.tcnj.edu/ . Qualifications Required: Have a Ph.D. in Communication Studies or a closely related field by the time of appointment. ABD candidates will be considered but must complete all degree requirements before starting the position. Demonstrate expertise in technology-mediated interpersonal or relational communication research. Show evidence of scholarly potential through publications, conference presentations, or dissertation research. Demonstrate knowledge of and commitment to best teaching practices. Demonstrate cultural competency and ability to foster inclusive learning environments and mutual respect for students and colleagues from diverse backgrounds. Preferred: We are especially interested in candidates whose research agenda complements and extends current faculty strengths within the department, opening possibilities for collaborative and interdisciplinary work. Persons with disabilities may request reasonable accommodations in order to perform the essential functions of the position. If the requested accommodation(s) cannot be made because it would cause the employer undue hardship, the applicant may not be eligible for the position. Employer Qualifications Employment at TCNJ is contingent upon the successful completion of an applicable background check, reference checks, and verification of identity and authorization to work in the United States (Form I-9). Accommodation: Applicants who require a reasonable accommodation to apply or interview should contact hr@tcnj.edu . Employee Benefits As a member of The College of New Jersey Community, you will be a part of an exciting and rewarding public college career. Eligible full-time employees will be able to take advantage of a generous benefits package that includes health, welfare, and retirement benefits, including: Comprehensive benefit plans covering medical, dental and prescription plans Generous leave entitlements program and Energy Savings Program Employee and dependent Tuition Waiver and Reimbursement Program Pension, retirement, and deferred compensation plans, group life insurance Employee Assistance Program (EAP) Employee affinity groups New Jersey State Employee Discount Program (Pet insurance, cell phone plan discounts, discounted amusement park tickets, etc.) Access to extensive learning opportunities To view a comprehensive list of benefits available to employees, visit our Health Benefits Plans and Programs page to learn more! How to Apply Applicants should submit: A cover letter highlighting how their qualifications match the requirements. A curriculum vitae. A teaching portfolio that includes a statement of teaching philosophy (no longer than two pages, single spaced) that addresses commitment to diversity and inclusive teaching, and evidence of teaching effectiveness, such as recent student evaluations, peer observation reports, or sample syllabi. A description of research interests and goals (no longer than two pages, single spaced). Unofficial transcripts (graduate and undergraduate). Names and contact information for at least three professional references. Applications should be submitted online . Please direct questions to the Chair of the Search Committee, Dr. Yachao Li, liya@tcnj.edu . Applications must be received by December 1 st to ensure full consideration. The search committee will begin reviewing applications immediately and continue until the position is filled. The College is committed to fostering a welcoming and inclusive campus community that respects and uplifts individuals from all backgrounds. We value the varied perspectives, experiences, and talents of all members of our community and strive to create an environment where everyone has equitable access to opportunities for success. As an equal opportunity employer, we comply with all applicable federal and state laws regarding nondiscrimination and affirmative action. We encourage applications from individuals whose lived experiences and professional interests align with our institutional mission of academic excellence, access, and integrity. Primary Location : Kendall Hall - Communication Studies Work Locations : Kendall Hall - Communication Studies 2000 Pennington Rd Ewing Township 08628 Job : Faculty Organization : The College of New Jersey Job Posting : Oct 7, 2026, 9:05:25 AM Copyright © 2020"
    },
    "https://tcnj.taleo.net/careersection/00_ex_faculty/jobdetail.ftl?job=26001072": {
      "title": "Clinical Specialist -Online Counselor Education",
      "description": "Job Description - Clinical Specialist -Online Counselor Education (26001072) Go to the main content section. Return to Careers Home Employment Opportunities Faculty Adjunct Faculty Staff/Administrative Internal Employment Student Employment Welcome. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Advanced Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Clinical Specialist -Online Counselor Education (26001072) Job Description Clinical Specialist -Online Counselor Education - ( 26001072 ) Description Appointment Type: Non-Tenure Track State Title: Clinical Specialist - 4 open positions Bargaining Unit: AFT Employment Type: 35 hours per week/Full-Time Expected Term: Start Date July 1, 2027 - June 30, 2030 Compensation: Range 24/$ 91,777.27 - $99,422.70 About TCNJ The College of New Jersey (TCNJ) is a highly selective institution that is consistently recognized as one of the top comprehensive colleges in the nation. Founded in 1855 as the New Jersey State Normal School, TCNJ maintains the eighth highest four-year graduation rate among all public colleges and universities. It is ranked by Money as one of the top 15 public colleges “most likely to pay off financially,” and U.S. News & World Report rates it the No. 1 public institution among regional universities in the northeast. About the Department: The Online Department of Counselor Education is a new department at The College of New Jersey, developed with external funding received for the next five years, with the expectation of the program being self-sustaining from that point forward. You will be foundational faculty growing a program that targets working with paraprofessionals in mental health HPSA communities to be able to complete their graduate education. Position Overview: The successful candidate will serve as a core counselor education program faculty member who is responsible for effective online teaching, advising, and professional activity in the field of counseling (sustained memberships in counseling associations, maintenance of certifications and/or licenses in counseling, sustained professional development and service to the profession). Teaching responsibilities will include ten courses over the academic year (fall, spring and summer terms). Our program has three 15-week terms with two 7-week sessions within each. You will be granted one 7-week session where you have no teaching responsibilities. All faculty are required to have a small active clinical practice. Candidates should be committed to inclusive excellence in higher education, demonstrated through, for example, culturally responsive course design and pedagogy, equity-minded student engagement and mentorship, and cultivating intercultural competencies needed for meaningful citizenship. TCNJ has a strong commitment to inclusive excellence in our community and to supporting a healthy work-life balance for our faculty. Candidates should be strongly committed to high quality online teaching and to fostering success for all students. Clinical Specialists will be expected to join a community committed to exploration and growth in pedagogical practices. TCNJ supports its community of teacher-scholars and practitioners through a range of internal grant programs, professional travel, engaging professional development programs, and other mechanisms. These intentional efforts support the recruitment, retention, and success of our faculty, particularly those from groups traditionally underrepresented in academe. Required Qualifications: Education: doctoral degree in counselor education; or have a related doctoral degree and have been employed as a full-time faculty member in a counselor education program for a minimum of one full academic year before July 1, 2013; or have been employed as a full-time doctoral-level faculty member in a CORE-accredited master’s program prior to July 1, 2017; or have graduated from a rehabilitation doctoral program prior to January 1, 2018. ABD candidates must have completed the PhD by the time the appointment begins. Demonstrate cultural competency and ability to foster inclusive learning environments and mutual respect for students and colleagues. Have an active, independent professional counseling license and two years or more of direct clinical experience outside of academia as a clinical mental health counselor. Priority will be given to those with community agency work experience, and/or deeper clinical experience. Experience teaching, preferably online, in a graduate program for counselor education. Proven record of excellence in instruction. Active clinical experience and independent license as a professional counselor. Strong commitment to working as part of a faculty team. Strong record of curriculum development. Record of active involvement in professional organizations. Proficiency in the CACREP accreditation requirements. Commitment to issues of social justice and diversity. Strong commitment to preparing students to become excellent practitioners. Preferred: H ave at least two years of teaching experience. Have earned the doctoral degree from a CACREP-accredited program. Persons with disabilities may request reasonable accommodations in order to perform the essential functions of the position. If the requested accommodation(s) cannot be made because it would cause the employer undue hardship, the applicant may not be eligible for the position. Employer Qualifications Employment at TCNJ is contingent upon the successful completion of an applicable background check, reference checks, and verification of identity and authorization to work in the United States (Form I-9). Accommodation: Applicants who require a reasonable accommodation to apply or interview should contact hr@tcnj.edu . Employee Benefits As a member of The College of New Jersey Community, you will be a part of an exciting and rewarding public college career. Eligible full-time employees will be able to take advantage of a generous benefits package that includes health, welfare, and retirement benefits, including: Comprehensive benefit plans covering medical, dental and prescription plans Generous leave entitlements program and Energy Savings Program Employee and dependent Tuition Waiver and Reimbursement Program Pension, retirement, and deferred compensation plans, group life insurance Employee Assistance Program (EAP) Employee affinity groups New Jersey State Employee Discount Program (Pet insurance, cell phone plan discounts, discounted amusement park tickets, etc.) Access to extensive learning opportunities To view a comprehensive list of benefits available to employees, visit our Health Benefits Plans and Programs page to learn more! How to Apply Candidates should submit (a) a letter of application highlighting their interest and qualifications, (b) a curriculum vitae, (c) a statement of teaching philosophy/approach (no longer than 2 pages), (d) a description of professional engagement and goals (no longer than 2 pages), (e) a statement of commitment to diversity, equity, and inclusion (no longer than 2 pages), (f) unofficial transcripts (graduate and undergraduate), (g) names and contact information for at least three professional references, (h) copy of your active, independent clinical license, and (i) copy of three recent student evaluations of teaching. Applications should be submitted electronically. Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the positions are filled. We would like to hire as soon as possible. Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. For full consideration, applications should be received by November 30 th , 2026. The College is committed to fostering a welcoming and inclusive campus community that respects and uplifts individuals from all backgrounds. We value the varied perspectives, experiences, and talents of all members of our community and strive to create an environment where everyone has equitable access to opportunities for success. As an equal opportunity employer, we comply with all applicable federal and state laws regarding nondiscrimination and affirmative action. We encourage applications from individuals whose lived experiences and professional interests align with our institutional mission of academic excellence, access, and integrity. Job : Faculty Organization : The College of New Jersey Job Posting : Sep 25, 2026, 8:07:01 AM Copyright © 2020"
    },
    "https://tcnj.taleo.net/careersection/00_ex_faculty/jobdetail.ftl?job=26001067": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor-Political Science",
      "description": "Job Description - Assistant Professor-Political Science (26001067) Go to the main content section. Return to Careers Home Employment Opportunities Faculty Adjunct Faculty Staff/Administrative Internal Employment Student Employment Welcome. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Advanced Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Assistant Professor-Political Science (26001067) Job Description Assistant Professor-Political Science - ( 26001067 ) Description State Title: Assistant Professor Appointment Type: Tenure Track Bargaining Unit: AFT Employment Type: 35 hours per week/Full-time Expected Term: August 7, 2027 - June 7, 2030 Compensation: Range 22/$ 90,190.21 - 97,129.13 About TCNJ The College of New Jersey (TCNJ) is a highly selective institution that is consistently recognized as one of the top comprehensive colleges in the nation. Founded in 1855 as the New Jersey State Normal School, TCNJ maintains the eighth highest four-year graduation rate among all public colleges and universities. It is ranked by Money as one of the top 15 public colleges “most likely to pay off financially,” and U.S. News & World Report rates it the No. 1 public institution among regional universities in the northeast. About the Department The Department of Political Science is a supportive and dynamic community of scholars and students. Political Science offers minors in public policy and pre-law, which draw students from across a wide range of academic disciplines, and we offer a Master’s degree in Public Policy. The Department currently has 6 tenured or tenure-track members. Over 140 students major in Political Science, over 130 minor in our programs, and another 30 major in the interdisciplinary International Studies program to which we contribute. For more information on the department, please visit: https://polisci.tcnj.edu/ Position Overview: We welcome candidates working in any area of IR. Candidates should demonstrate an active and rigorous research agenda in their area of specialization and be prepared to teach Introduction to International Relations, US Foreign Policy, and courses within their own specialization, as well as contribute to the Department's research course sequence. The successful candidate will excel in the classroom and seek ways to integrate their scholarship and teaching, consistent with the Department's teacher-scholar model. The typical teaching load is three courses per semester. All new tenure-track faculty members receive one course release per year, in two of their first three years, to support their scholarship. A PhD is preferred, but the College will consider ABDs if the degree will be granted by time of appointment. Applications received by November 1 will receive full consideration. The Department of Political Science at The College of New Jersey (TCNJ) invites applications for a tenure-track position in International Relations (IR) at the rank of Assistant Professor to join our community in August 2027. Persons with disabilities may request reasonable accommodations in order to perform the essential functions of the position. If the requested accommodation(s) cannot be made because it would cause the employer undue hardship, the applicant may not be eligible for the position. Employer Qualifications Employment at TCNJ is contingent upon the successful completion of an applicable background check, reference checks, and verification of identity and authorization to work in the United States (Form I-9). Accommodation: Applicants who require a reasonable accommodation to apply or interview should contact hr@tcnj.edu . Employee Benefits As a member of The College of New Jersey Community, you will be a part of an exciting and rewarding public college career. Eligible full-time employees will be able to take advantage of a generous benefits package that includes health, welfare, and retirement benefits, including: Comprehensive benefit plans covering medical, dental and prescription plans Generous leave entitlements program and Energy Savings Program Employee and dependent Tuition Waiver and Reimbursement Program Pension, retirement, and deferred compensation plans, group life insurance Employee Assistance Program (EAP) Employee affinity groups New Jersey State Employee Discount Program (Pet insurance, cell phone plan discounts, discounted amusement park tickets, etc.) Access to extensive learning opportunities To view a comprehensive list of benefits available to employees, visit our Health Benefits Plans and Programs page to learn more! How to Apply Applicants should submit the following materials using the online application system at: 1) a cover letter describing qualifications and research and teaching interests, 2) curriculum vitae, 3) one scholarly writing sample, 4) evidence of teaching effectiveness (including student evaluations and syllabi if available), 5) a statement on teaching philosophy (no longer than one page), and 5) a statement on how diversity and inclusion are incorporated into their work as teachers, scholars, and mentors (no longer than one page), and 6) names and contact information for three professional references. Applications should be submitted electronically online. Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. For full consideration, applications should be received by November 1, 2026. Any questions can be directed to Sarah Chartock, International Relations Search Committee Chair, at irpolsearch@tcnj.edu. The College is committed to fostering a welcoming and inclusive campus community that respects and uplifts individuals from all backgrounds. We value the varied perspectives, experiences, and talents of all members of our community and strive to create an environment where everyone has equitable access to opportunities for success. As an equal opportunity employer, we comply with all applicable federal and state laws regarding nondiscrimination and affirmative action. We encourage applications from individuals whose lived experiences and professional interests align with our institutional mission of academic excellence, access, and integrity. Primary Location : Social Sciences - Political Science Work Locations : Social Sciences - Political Science 2000 Pennington Rd Ewing Township 08628 Job : Faculty Organization : The College of New Jersey Job Posting : Sep 21, 2026, 9:56:44 AM Copyright © 2020"
    },
    "https://tcnj.taleo.net/careersection/00_ex_faculty/jobdetail.ftl?job=26000823": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor-Civil Engineering",
      "description": "Job Description - Assistant Professor-Civil Engineering (26000823) Go to the main content section. Return to Careers Home Employment Opportunities Faculty Adjunct Faculty Staff/Administrative Internal Employment Student Employment Welcome. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Advanced Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Assistant Professor-Civil Engineering (26000823) Job Description Assistant Professor-Civil Engineering - ( 26000823 ) Description Appointment Type: Tenure Track State Title: Assistant Professor Bargaining Unit: AFT Employment Type: 35 Hours per week/Full-time Expected Term: 08/07/2027 - 06/07/2030 Compensation: Range 25 /$ 108,433.95 - $ 116,469.62 About TCNJ The College of New Jersey (TCNJ) is a highly selective institution that is consistently recognized as one of the top comprehensive colleges in the nation. Founded in 1855 as the New Jersey State Normal School, TCNJ maintains the eighth highest four-year graduation rate among all public colleges and universities. It is ranked by Money as one of the top 15 public colleges “most likely to pay off financially,” and U.S. News & World Report rates it the No. 1 public institution among regional universities in the northeast. The Department of Civil Engineering at The College of New Jersey (TCNJ) invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track position in Transportation Engineering at the rank of Assistant Professor , beginning Fall 2027. Position Overview: We seek a transportation engineer who will contribute to our undergraduate transportation curriculum while developing teaching and scholarship in transportation systems analysis, planning, and data informed decision making. The successful candidate will share responsibility for the department's core transportation engineering curriculum and will have opportunities to develop advanced undergraduate coursework reflecting their technical and scholarly interests. Areas of particular interest include transportation systems analysis, transportation planning, traffic operations, transportation safety, intelligent transportation systems, infrastructure systems, and the application of probability, statistics, optimization, or data analytics to transportation engineering. Candidates with complementary expertise in other areas of transportation engineering are also encouraged to apply. The Civil Engineering Department emphasizes rigorous undergraduate engineering education, close interaction between faculty and students, and integration of engineering analysis, design, and professional practice. The successful candidate will be expected to teach undergraduate transportation engineering planning and design courses, contribute to instruction in civil engineering probability and statistics or related analytical topics, advise senior design projects, mentor undergraduate research, and develop advanced coursework in their area of expertise. The successful candidate will also be expected to establish or maintain a sustainable program of scholarly activity appropriate to TCNJ's teacher-scholar model. Opportunities exist for interdisciplinary collaboration with faculty across the School of Engineering and the College, including work involving transportation, infrastructure systems, sustainability, sensing, data analytics, and related areas. Engagement with government agencies, industry, and the engineering profession is encouraged. Candidates must have an earned doctorate in Civil Engineering, Transportation Engineering, or a closely related field by the time of appointment. Candidates should demonstrate the potential for excellence in teaching and scholarly activity. Professional engineering licensure, progress toward licensure, and relevant professional practice, government, or consulting experience are valued. The Department of Civil Engineering offers an ABET-accredited undergraduate program with strong student demand and excellent post-graduation outcomes. Faculty work closely with students throughout the curriculum, including classroom instruction, laboratory and design experiences, undergraduate research, and senior capstone projects. The successful candidate will join an established transportation program and help shape its continued development in transportation systems analysis and planning. Persons with disabilities may request reasonable accommodations in order to perform the essential functions of the position. If the requested accommodation(s) cannot be made because it would cause the employer undue hardship, the applicant may not be eligible for the position. Employer Qualifications Employment at TCNJ is contingent upon the successful completion of an applicable background check, reference checks, and verification of identity and authorization to work in the United States (Form I-9). Accommodation: Applicants who require a reasonable accommodation to apply or interview should contact hr@tcnj.edu . Employee Benefits As a member of The College of New Jersey Community, you will be a part of an exciting and rewarding public college career. Eligible full-time employees will be able to take advantage of a generous benefits package that includes health, welfare, and retirement benefits, including: Comprehensive benefit plans covering medical, dental and prescription plans Generous leave entitlements program and Energy Savings Program Employee and dependent Tuition Waiver and Reimbursement Program Pension, retirement, and deferred compensation plans, group life insurance Employee Assistance Program (EAP) Employee affinity groups New Jersey State Employee Discount Program (Pet insurance, cell phone plan discounts, discounted amusement park tickets, etc.) Access to extensive learning opportunities To view a comprehensive list of benefits available to employees, visit our Health Benefits Plans and Programs page to learn more! How to Apply Applicants should submit: ● A curriculum vitae; ● A cover letter, in formal letter format, describing the candidate's interest in the position and how their teaching, scholarship, professional experience, and approach to mentoring students would contribute to TCNJ and the Civil Engineering Department; ● A teaching statement describing the candidate's teaching interests and approach to undergraduate engineering education; ● A research statement describing the candidate's scholarly interests, future research plans, opportunities for undergraduate student involvement, and how they can complement and enhance current research in the department and school; and ● Contact information for three professional references. For best consideration, please submit all materials by November 15, 2026. The College is committed to fostering a welcoming and inclusive campus community that respects and uplifts individuals from all backgrounds. We value the varied perspectives, experiences, and talents of all members of our community and strive to create an environment where everyone has equitable access to opportunities for success. As an equal opportunity employer, we comply with all applicable federal and state laws regarding nondiscrimination and affirmative action. We encourage applications from individuals whose lived experiences and professional interests align with our institutional mission of academic excellence, access, and integrity. Primary Location : Armstrong Hall - Engineering Work Locations : Armstrong Hall - Engineering 2000 Pennington Rd Ewing Township 08628 Job : Faculty Organization : The College of New Jersey Job Posting : Sep 16, 2026, 1:03:13 PM Copyright © 2020"
    },
    "https://tcnj.taleo.net/careersection/00_ex_faculty/jobdetail.ftl?job=26001068": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor-Psychology",
      "description": "Job Description - Assistant Professor-Psychology (26001068) Go to the main content section. Return to Careers Home Employment Opportunities Faculty Adjunct Faculty Staff/Administrative Internal Employment Student Employment Welcome. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Advanced Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Assistant Professor-Psychology (26001068) Job Description Assistant Professor-Psychology - ( 26001068 ) Description Appointment Type: Tenure Track State Title: Assistant Professor Bargaining Unit: AFT Employment Type: 35 hours per week/Full-time Expected Term: 8/7/2027 - 6/7/2030 Compensation: Range 22/$90,190.21 - $97,129.13 About TCNJ The College of New Jersey (TCNJ) is a highly selective institution that is consistently recognized as one of the top comprehensive colleges in the nation. Founded in 1855 as the New Jersey State Normal School, TCNJ maintains the eighth highest four-year graduation rate among all public colleges and universities. It is ranked by Money as one of the top 15 public colleges “most likely to pay off financially,” and U.S. News & World Report rates it the No. 1 public institution among regional universities in the Northeast. About the Department: The Department of Psychology at The College of New Jersey (TCNJ) invites applications for a 10-month, tenure-track Assistant Professor position in Industrial/Organizational Psychology to join our community starting in August 2027. The Department of Psychology has 19 tenure-line faculty members and approximately 750 majors. We are a collaborative and collegial community of faculty, staff, students, and alumni who value the processes of critical inquiry and discovery in the laboratory, the classroom, and the community. Consistent with the mission of the School of Humanities and Social Sciences, we strive to provide experiences through which our students can become analytical, critical, and creative thinkers, conscientious and active global citizens, and lifelong learners and leaders. Through the entwined roles of teaching and scholarship, we strive to prepare our students to contribute to their communities and pursue their chosen careers. The Department is deeply committed to fostering learning and professional development opportunities for all of its students, including through faculty-mentored research and internships. For more information about the department, visit https://psychology.tcnj.edu Position Overview: We seek a colleague with the potential or demonstrated ability to effectively teach and conduct research with undergraduate students in the area of Industrial/Organizational Psychology. The standard teaching load is 3 courses per semester. All new tenure-track faculty members receive one course release per year in two of their first three years to support their scholarship. The successful candidate will be prepared to teach Organizational Psychology, Industrial Psychology, and research methods or statistics, as well as an advanced undergraduate seminar in their area of expertise. The successful candidate will also be prepared to develop and lead a research lab with undergraduate students that will count as a course in their teaching load. Candidates should be committed to inclusive excellence in higher education, demonstrated through, for example , culturally responsive course design and pedagogy, equity-minded student engagement and mentorship, and cultivating intercultural competencies needed for meaningful citizenship. TCNJ’s faculty reappointment and promotion standards for teaching and service are articulated in the College’s Reappointment and Promotions Document, and the standards for scholarship are available in the Psychology Department’s Disciplinary Standards Document . Faculty are represented by American Federation of Teachers Local 2364 , which belongs to the Council of New Jersey State College Locals . TCNJ has a strong commitment to inclusive excellence in our community and to supporting a healthy work-life balance for our faculty of teacher-scholars. Teaching and research are mutually supportive activities at TCNJ. Candidates should be strongly committed to the teacher-scholar model, to maintaining both high-quality teaching and an active and productive program of scholarship, and to encouraging and mentoring highly motivated students in intensive work both inside and outside the classroom. They also serve as academic advisors and have service responsibilities within their department, school, and the college. Although not required for tenure and promotion, faculty are encouraged and supported in seeking external funding consistent with this mission. TCNJ supports its community of teacher-scholars through a progressive faculty workload model, internal grant and sabbatical programs, funds for professional travel, engaging professional development programs, and other mechanisms. These intentional efforts support the recruitment, retention, and success of our faculty, particularly our teacher-scholars from groups traditionally underrepresented in academe. Qualifications: Required: ●     Have a PhD in Industrial/Organizational Psychology or a closely related field. ABDs will be considered only if all requirements for their degree will be completed prior to the start date. ●     Have the potential or demonstrated ability to effectively teach Psychology courses at the undergraduate level in Industrial/Organizational Psychology, research methods, and/or statistics. ●     Have a related record of peer-reviewed publications and a research agenda that is clearly defined, shows promise, and can involve undergraduate student researchers. ●     Demonstrate cultural competency and ability to foster inclusive learning environments and mutual respect for students and colleagues. Persons with disabilities may request reasonable accommodations in order to perform the essential functions of the position. If the requested accommodation(s) cannot be made because it would cause the employer undue hardship, the applicant may not be eligible for the position. Employer Qualifications Employment at TCNJ is contingent upon the successful completion of an applicable background check, reference checks, and verification of identity and authorization to work in the United States (Form I-9). Accommodation: Applicants who require a reasonable accommodation to apply or interview should contact hr@tcnj.edu . Employee Benefits As a member of The College of New Jersey Community, you will be a part of an exciting and rewarding public college career. Eligible full-time employees will be able to take advantage of a generous benefits package that includes health, welfare, and retirement benefits, including: Comprehensive benefit plans covering medical, dental, and prescription plans Generous leave entitlements program and Energy Savings Program Employee and dependent Tuition Waiver and Reimbursement Program Pension, retirement, and deferred compensation plans, group life insurance Employee Assistance Program (EAP) Employee affinity groups New Jersey State Employee Discount Program (Pet insurance, cell phone plan discounts, discounted amusement park tickets, etc.) Access to extensive learning opportunities To view a comprehensive list of benefits available to employees, visit our Health Benefits Plans and Programs page to learn more! How to Apply Candidates should submit (a) a letter of application highlighting their interest and qualifications, (b) a curriculum vitae, (c) a statement of teaching philosophy/approach (no longer than 2 pages), (d) a description of research interests and goals (no longer than 2 pages), (e) a statement of commitment to diversity, equity, and inclusion (no longer than 1 page), (f) unofficial transcripts (graduate and undergraduate), and (g) names and contact information for three professional references. Applications should be submitted electronically online. Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. For full consideration, applications should be received by October 20, 2026. The College is committed to fostering a welcoming and inclusive campus community that respects and uplifts individuals from all backgrounds. We value the varied perspectives, experiences, and talents of all members of our community and strive to create an environment where everyone has equitable access to opportunities for success. As an equal opportunity employer, we comply with all applicable federal and state laws regarding nondiscrimination and affirmative action. We encourage applications from individuals whose lived experiences and professional interests align with our institutional mission of academic excellence, access, and integrity. Primary Location : Social Sciences - Psychology Work Locations : Social Sciences - Psychology 2000 Pennington Rd Ewing Township 08628 Job : Faculty Organization : The College of New Jersey Job Posting : Sep 16, 2026, 7:23:23 AM Copyright © 2020"
    },
    "https://tcnj.taleo.net/careersection/00_ex_faculty/jobdetail.ftl?job=26000828": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor-Biology",
      "description": "Job Description - Assistant Professor-Biology (26000828) Go to the main content section. Return to Careers Home Employment Opportunities Faculty Adjunct Faculty Staff/Administrative Internal Employment Student Employment Welcome. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Advanced Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Assistant Professor-Biology (26000828) Job Description Assistant Professor-Biology - ( 26000828 ) Description Appointment Type: Tenure Track State Title: Assistant Professor Bargaining Unit: AFT Employment Type: 35 Hours per week/Full-time Expected Term: 08/07/2027 - 06/07/2030 Compensation: Range 22/$ 93,659.67 - $ 100,598.59 About The College of New Jersey: Founded in 1855, TCNJ is a selective public institution that has earned national recognition for its commitment to excellence. TCNJ enrolls approximately 8,200 students, including 7,433 undergraduates and 855 graduate students, 27% of whom are self-described as members of groups traditionally underrepresented in academe. Strong curricular and co-curricular programming have helped foster a first-year to sophomore retention rate of 89.7%, a 4-year graduation rate of 74% and a 6-year graduation rate of 85% (among the highest in the country). Five signature experiences are the hallmark of a TCNJ education: a personalized, collaborative, and rigorous education; undergraduate research, mentored internships, and field experiences; community engaged learning; global engagement; and leadership development. TCNJ has also received national recognition for the adoption and promotion of the teacher-scholar model for our faculty. A strong liberal arts core forms the foundation for programs offered through TCNJ’s seven academic schools—Arts and Communication; Business; Education; Engineering; Humanities and Social Sciences; Nursing and Health Sciences; and Science. TCNJ has a strong Phi Beta Kappa chapter—an honor shared by less than 10 percent of colleges and universities nationally. Among other initiatives, a series of faculty/staff-based affinity groups (e.g., Minority Executive Council, Women’s Professional Network, Parent and Family Network, TCNJ PRIDE) supports a welcoming, supportive, and inclusive environment at TCNJ. TCNJ is located within an hour of New York City and Philadelphia. The College’s campus is set on 289 tree-lined acres in suburban Ewing Township and is known for its natural beauty. In addition to its growing racial and ethnic diversity, the region offers excellent public schools, prestigious medical centers, restaurants, art and entertainment, as well as numerous cultural and recreational activities. For more information about the college, please visit: http://www.tcnj.edu/ . About the Department: Our new colleague will join a department of 16 full-time faculty, who are deeply engaged across the discipline of biology. The Biology Department is housed in a dedicated building and is home to approximately 500 undergraduate majors, while providing learning opportunities in biology for students across campus. Our faculty members make use of state-of-the-art tools and techniques in classroom and research spaces, often attending regional and national conferences and/or publishing with undergraduate collaborators. Our faculty frequently participate in the TCNJ Mentored Undergraduate Summer Experience, an 8-week summer undergraduate research program that provides stipends and housing for students. Many faculty are successful at obtaining grants from federal and private funding agencies with the support of a dedicated grant writer in the TCNJ School of Science. Our curriculum has recently undergone extensive revision as part of our HHMI Inclusive Excellence award, resulting in the use of scientific teaching and inclusive pedagogy throughout our curriculum. The Biology community hosts a regular colloquium series as well as many community-building events throughout the academic year. The Department of Biology at The College of New Jersey (TCNJ) invites applications for a 10-month, tenure-track Assistant Professor position in Global Change Biology to join our community starting in August 202 7. Position Overview: We welcome applicants who will build a productive research program asking questions about human impacts on biological systems and involving undergraduates, and who will be passionate about teaching at a primarily undergraduate, residential, liberal arts-centered institution. We are particularly interested in candidates whose research is interdisciplinary and integrates multiple levels of biological complexity. Research interests could include, but are not limited to, community ecology (terrestrial or marine), invasive species biology, computational biology, plant biology, ecotoxicology and more. A research program that provides meaningful fieldwork experiences for our students is preferred, but not required. Our new colleague will join an active department of faculty deeply engaged in research programs ranging from microbes to ecosystems who make use of state-of-the-art tools and techniques while publishing with undergraduate collaborators. The successful candidate will teach Foundations of Biological Inquiry, a one-semester introductory biology course designed to actively engage students in core concepts and competencies in biology and informed by best practices in scientific teaching. Teaching responsibilities also include additional courses of the candidate’s design in their area of expertise, offered during semesters when not teaching introductory biology. Note that all areas of biological inquiry will be considered, but particular value will be placed on courses that complement or build upon the existing curriculum . Can didates should be committed to inclusive excellence in higher education demonstrated through, for example, culturally responsive pedagogy and equity-minded student engagement. The successful applicant will receive a start-up package, have a dedicated research space, and can access department-maintained facilities that include an ecology workroom; Scientific Computing Center with high performance computing cluster maintained by a dedicated staff member; an animal facility, environmental growth chambers, and greenhouse; state-of-the art microscopy facilities (field emission SEM with cryopreparation unit and cryostage, a spinning disk confocal microscope with microfluidic temperature control, motorized fluorescent dissecting microscope with a multiple objective heads and transmitted light base) ; molecular biology equipment (quantitative PCR machine, Tecan plate reader and additional core molecular biology equipment); autoclaves, cold room, ultra-low temp freezers, and biosafety and laminar flow hoods. We are interested in candidates whose research and teaching will connect and integrate with other disciplines (including but not limited to environmental studies, chemistry/biochemistry, public health, computer science, and physics) and who have the potential to contribute collaboratively to interdisciplinary curricular and scholarly efforts supported by School of Science initiatives . Qualifications: Required: Have a PhD in Biology, Ecology, or a closely related field . ABDs will be considered only if the degree will be completed prior to the start date. Have a record of peer-reviewed publication(s) in their area of expertise. Present either evidence or promise of excellence in undergraduate teaching and mentoring. Articulate a vision for a productive research program related to global change biology that includes undergraduates in a meaningful way. Demonstrate an ability to communicate science effectively in oral and written formats and to varied audiences. Demonstrate cultural competency and ability to foster inclusive learning environments , mutual respect for students and colleagues, and the potential to mentor minoritized students effectively. Preferred: Post-doctoral research experience. Use of interdisciplinary approaches in their scholarly research. Have a record of peer-reviewed publication(s) related to the proposed area of study. Ability to provide meaningful fieldwork experiences to undergraduates within the context of their scholarly program. Classroom and laboratory teaching experience, preferably with undergraduates, and in biology or a closely related field. Persons with disabilities may request reasonable accommodations in order to perform the essential functions of the position. If the requested accommodation(s) cannot be made because it would cause the employer undue hardship, the applicant may not be eligible for the position. Employer Qualifications Employment at TCNJ is contingent upon the successful completion of an applicable background check, reference checks, and verification of identity and authorization to work in the United States (Form I-9). Accommodation: Applicants who require a reasonable accommodation to apply or interview should contact hr@tcnj.edu . Employee Benefits As a member of The College of New Jersey Community, you will be a part of an exciting and rewarding public college career. Eligible full-time employees will be able to take advantage of a generous benefits package that includes health, welfare, and retirement benefits, including: Comprehensive benefit plans covering medical, dental and prescription plans Generous leave entitlements program and Energy Savings Program Employee and dependent Tuition Waiver and Reimbursement Program Pension, retirement, and deferred compensation plans, group life insurance Employee Assistance Program (EAP) Employee affinity groups New Jersey State Employee Discount Program (Pet insurance, cell phone plan discounts, discounted amusement park tickets, etc.) Access to extensive learning opportunities To view a comprehensive list of benefits available to employees, visit our Health Benefits Plans and Programs page to learn more! How to Apply Candidates should submit (a) a letter of application highlighting relevant intere st and qualifications, (b) a curriculum vitae, (c) a statement of teaching philosophy/approach (no longer than 2 pages) , (d) a description of research interests and goals (no longer than 3 pages), (e) a statement on your approach to inclusive teaching and mentoring that aligns with TCNJ’s mission ( no longer than 2 pages ) , (f) unofficial transcripts (graduate and undergraduate), and (g) names and contact information for at least three professional references. Applications should be submitted electronically through our Taleo system. Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. For full consideration, applications should be received by September 1, 2026. The College is committed to fostering a welcoming and inclusive campus community that respects and uplifts individuals from all backgrounds. We value the varied perspectives, experiences, and talents of all members of our community and strive to create an environment where everyone has equitable access to opportunities for success. As an equal opportunity employer, we comply with all applicable federal and state laws regarding nondiscrimination and affirmative action. We encourage applications from individuals whose lived experiences and professional interests align with our institutional mission of academic excellence, access, and integrity. Primary Location : Biology Building - Biology Work Locations : Biology Building - Biology 2000 Pennington Rd Ewing Township 08628 Job : Faculty Organization : The College of New Jersey Job Posting : Jul 30, 2026, 11:40:31 AM Copyright © 2020"
    },
    "https://tcnj.taleo.net/careersection/00_ex_faculty/jobdetail.ftl?job=26000644": {
      "title": "Visiting Assistant Professor-Kinesiology & Health Sciences",
      "description": "Job Description - Visiting Assistant Professor-Kinesiology & Health Sciences (26000644) Go to the main content section. Return to Careers Home Employment Opportunities Faculty Adjunct Faculty Staff/Administrative Internal Employment Student Employment Welcome. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Advanced Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Visiting Assistant Professor-Kinesiology & Health Sciences (26000644) Job Description Visiting Assistant Professor-Kinesiology & Health Sciences - ( 26000644 ) Description Appointment Type: Visiting Assistant Professor/Temporary State Title: Assistant Professor Bargaining Unit: AFT Employment Type: 35 Hours per week/Full-time Expected Term: August 8, 2026 - June 11, 2027 Compensation: Range 22/$ 86,720.75 - $ 93,659.67 About TCNJ The College of New Jersey (TCNJ) is a highly selective institution that is consistently recognized as one of the top comprehensive colleges in the nation. Founded in 1855 as the New Jersey State Normal School, TCNJ maintains the eighth highest four-year graduation rate among all public colleges and universities. It is ranked by Money as one of the top 15 public colleges “most likely to pay off financially,” and U.S. News & World Report rates it the No. 1 public institution among regional universities in the northeast. Position Overview: The College of New Jersey (TCNJ ) invites applications for a one-year teaching position in the Department of Kinesiology and Health Sciences. Candidates should demonstrate potential to become an innovative teacher-scholar, whose research, educational, and professional experiences have prepared them to contribute meaningfully to an evidence-based movement science program/curriculum. The candidate’s area of research specialization is open; however, the candidate should be prepared to teach in areas related to health & wellness strength & conditioning, exercise behavioral sciences, metabolic nutrition, exercise science, leadership management, data analytics, bio-mechanics, or other general kinesiology courses that support CoAES and CASCE accreditation. The successful candidate will teach four courses each semester. The position carries minimal ex pectations of service or advising so that the candidate may focus on teaching and on developing effective and engaging pedagogical strategies and state of the art student laboratory opportunities. In that regard, the candidate will be mentored by the Department Chair and further supported by TCNJ’s Center for Excellence in Teaching and Learning. Qualifications: Required: Have obtained a Ph.D. in Exercise Science (or a closely related field). Consideration may be provided to advanced ABD candidates. Demonstrate commitment to excellence in teaching at the undergraduate level. Show evidence of ability to teach within a Kinesiology and Health Science through publications, conference presentations, dissertation research, teaching, or other educational or professional experiences. Have strong communication skills in writing, speaking, and presenting with a teaching/learning philosophy that reflects a diversity of thought and experience. Demonstrate cultural competency and ability to foster inclusive learning environments and mutual respect for students and colleagues from diverse backgrounds. Persons with disabilities may request reasonable accommodations in order to perform the essential functions of the position. If the requested accommodation(s) cannot be made because it would cause the employer undue hardship, the applicant may not be eligible for the position. Employer Qualifications Employment at TCNJ is contingent upon the successful completion of an applicable background check, reference checks, and verification of identity and authorization to work in the United States (Form I-9). Accommodation: Applicants who require a reasonable accommodation to apply or interview should contact hr@tcnj.edu . Employee Benefits As a member of The College of New Jersey Community, you will be a part of an exciting and rewarding public college career. Eligible full-time employees will be able to take advantage of a generous benefits package that includes health, welfare, and retirement benefits, including: Comprehensive benefit plans covering medical, dental and prescription plans Generous leave entitlements program and Energy Savings Program Employee and dependent Tuition Waiver and Reimbursement Program Pension, retirement, and deferred compensation plans, group life insurance Employee Assistance Program (EAP) Employee affinity groups New Jersey State Employee Discount Program (Pet insurance, cell phone plan discounts, discounted amusement park tickets, etc.) Access to extensive learning opportunities To view a comprehensive list of benefits available to employees, visit our Health Benefits Plans and Programs page to learn more! How to Apply Applicants should submit: A cover letter highlighting how their qualifications match the requirements. A curriculum vitae. A statement of teaching philosophy that demonstrates commitment to diversity, equity, and inclusion (no longer than one page, single-spaced). Names and contact information for at least three professional references. Applications should be submitted electronically. Applications received by July 30th will receive immediate and full consideration, with ongoing application review until the position is filled. Please direct questions to the Chair of the Search Committee, Dr. Anne Farrell, afarrell@tcnj.edu. For information on the Department of Kinesiology and Health Sciences, please visit https://khs.tcnj.edu/ Primary Location: Department of Kinesiology and Health Sciences- Packer Hall, Second Floor. Work Locations: 2000 Pennington Rd Ewing Township 08628 Job: Faculty Organization: The College of New Jersey The College is committed to fostering a welcoming and inclusive campus community that respects and uplifts individuals from all backgrounds. We value the varied perspectives, experiences, and talents of all members of our community and strive to create an environment where everyone has equitable access to opportunities for success. As an equal opportunity employer, we comply with all applicable federal and state laws regarding nondiscrimination and affirmative action. We encourage applications from individuals whose lived experiences and professional interests align with our institutional mission of academic excellence, access, and integrity. Primary Location : Packer Hall - Health & Exercise Science Work Locations : Packer Hall - Health & Exercise Science 2000 Pennington Rd Ewing Township 08628 Job : Faculty Organization : The College of New Jersey Job Posting : Jul 22, 2026, 7:08:12 AM Copyright © 2020"
    }
  },
